<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:56:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>UK PM Burnham seeks 'hope again' at Labour Party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:14202bd67bcc136c7cf573e4d119f4981c8dd9ef43dd2f5fe84964a486b1e560</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376--71e603fc9e60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham is seeking a delicate balance between optimism and realism at Labour's annual party conference. He promised hope and an end to "politics as usual" but also an "honest conversation" about difficult dilemmas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01ad9355d1ad254cbc3e276d2510a4c6fb9fecf74fba29cdbf94d4e36e0dedfb</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach as they try to rebuild their lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8fe5aea548be2b2a95dd11960e225d91931ea9a613a0dc55091384d161f8a7f</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--3aa02594713a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach-as-they-try-to-rebuild-their-lives/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: As corruption cases multiply, experts question whether the anti-corruption drive is addressing the causes or just the symptoms.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efbcaf65271cd54cd4c9ba5dd81f880e7ee40bc37958d06876594b4f91f47805</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:26Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressin/a-79473031--8c7e71b0b3b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressing-the-causes-or-just-the-symptoms/a-79473031?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a former president to the ex-intelligence chief, Albania is prosecuting senior officials at a rate once thought impossible. But do more prosecutions mean less corruption or simply better enforcement?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iraq: US troops withdraw from their Iraqi US-led Operation Inherent Resolve mission against ISIS after 12 years as Baghdad delays militia disarmament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efee098cb47ec1d0ff2342ac8875e0f8c06538207bc77e165d6e761f34646603</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T11:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iraq-us-troops-withdraw-from-their-iraqi-us-led-operation-inherent-resolve-mission-against-isis-afte/a-79462926--5b2f211b74d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iraq-us-troops-withdraw-from-their-iraqi-us-led-operation-inherent-resolve-mission-against-isis-after-12-years-as-baghdad-delays-militia-disarmament/a-79462926?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US completes its military withdrawal from Iraq, Baghdad declares a new era of sovereignty. But as US troops leave, questions remain over militias, foreign forces and the country's future security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia repatriates Myanmar migrants despite UN warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c74225344919f468ba8d48b12983e3459eef5e31d99b42c2e3788f8bb8197db</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/malaysia-repatriates-myanmar-migrants-despite-un-warnings/a-79470814--e0fb5ad7aea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/malaysia-repatriates-myanmar-migrants-despite-un-warnings/a-79470814?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Malaysia has started repatriating about 1,500 Myanmar nationals, defying warnings from the UN and rights groups. Malaysia, facing an uptick in anti-migrant sentiment, says the program is strictly voluntary.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: US government questions bail for Fairford base suspects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98bb8a722fc05392c43fda688029253664ff6493aa86e18bf77297371b2faf77</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:55:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803--3794b4b54f63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US government sees "the hand of a foreign actor" in the security scare at RAF Fairford, a hub for US heavy bombers in Europe. Donald Trump criticized the suspects being released on bail amid ongoing investigations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions on Iran's aviation industry make travel less predictable as countries cancel flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af8d77035a69991f7ab83f9354abc5c2a2f56a29a4128248e1961b1868db7984</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T00:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-on-iran-s-aviation-industry-make-travel-less-predictable-as-countries-cancel-flights/a-79459140--66d2076cb57a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-on-iran-s-aviation-industry-make-travel-less-predictable-as-countries-cancel-flights/a-79459140?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The threat of secondary US sanctions is putting pressure on airports, fuel suppliers and aviation companies that service Iranian airlines. Some countries have already canceled flights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian human rights lawyer Nasrin Sotoudeh wins the 2026 Vaclav Havel Human Rights Prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83a733f42d3907a81f0558ab0affe1e1456a0d02e0b6316ddb677bc0ac78102c</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T16:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-human-rights-lawyer-nasrin-sotoudeh-wins-the-2026-vaclav-havel-human-rights-prize/a-79462111--5437e6d160e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-human-rights-lawyer-nasrin-sotoudeh-wins-the-2026-vaclav-havel-human-rights-prize/a-79462111?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Council of Europe awarded human rights lawyer Nasrin Sotoudeh with the Vaclav Havel human rights prize. She is a prominent advocate for the rights of women, children and political prisoners.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sicily: Mount Etna ash disrupts Catania flights again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f1f8a5e0293ec00cb09971be7cdd6a26797dcbe32ab6c3dae9bfa39f73e93fb</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773--6d2664a469ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sicily-mount-etna-ash-disrupts-catania-flights-again/a-79462773?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A thick ash cloud from Mount Etna has been disrupting flights to Catania in Sicily for several days. Italy and Europe's most active volcano, Etna has impacted air travel several times this summer.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Comedian convicted for 'insulting' Erdogan in show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76fdca5246ade9209ebbed9a744409c467bcb98c43b84f4c8d4fe11d91cecfe2</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759--b32d8c83cb81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-comedian-convicted-for-insulting-erdogan-in-show/a-79455759?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Deniz Goktas was convicted of two of three charges, including "insulting" the president, but was released pending the appeal process. Nominally, Turkey is a secular country with free speech.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's youth-led Cockroach movement targets election chief over voter-roll dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5a9c16dbfb80c57e28ed4f05b09ef91a19f598f8fdb7f4c7107398014136acd</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:56:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-targets-election-chief-over-voter-roll-dispute/a-79462036--b918a132d9c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-targets-election-chief-over-voter-roll-dispute/a-79462036?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Cockroach movement has emerged as an influential force in Indian politics. Its latest campaign targets the election commission amid a wider debate over voter rolls and public trust in electoral institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Avalanche in Nepal leaves 2 dead, several missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51f077b8c45a0417659d228ee27b7f7314fe464a12cc68f51161bd026e5649ff</id><updated>2026-09-29T14:54:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101--fcbca2d1e804.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An avalanche has struck the Himlung Himal base camp in Nepal after days of severe weather. Two guides are confirmed dead and at least 14 people remain missing in the remote region.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
